WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.512
Some of the most powerful steps don't
belong to DBAs at all, by design.

2
00:00:04.512 --> 00:00:09.284
Granting the instance identity its
directory permissions takes a role that can

3
00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:11.489
manage every other role in the tenant,

4
00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:15.259
so it stays with a small identity
group, eligible only on request.

5
00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:19.310
And the Azure roles around the server
now matter as much as sysadmin.

6
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.737
Contributor on the server can
run privileged extensions.

7
00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:27.331
Contributor on the SQL resource
can switch SQL logins back on.

8
00:00:27.331 --> 00:00:30.413
Whoever holds those roles
holds a database privilege.

9
00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:33.869
So the CISO's decision: review
those Azure assignments on

10
00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:37.401
the same cadence as sysadmin,
from the first Arc onboarding.

11
00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:39.770
Next, the applications upstream.
